Z||000010||ig88vsbobafett||12-29-2001||11:02 AM||||Yeah ok  know i am going to get chewed out for this but i have a manual 4speed in it now what is needed to go to a 3 apeed auto <BR>i have access to a free 3 speed auto from a 86 buick century||||reg||1
Z||000011||mrfiero||12-29-2001||03:09 PM||||Swapping over to an auto. is a very involved process......it's more than just installing teh tranny.  You'll have wiring issues, ECM issues,radiator issues, etc.<P>I am looking to get $50 for the Isuzu 5-sp. that I have.  That includes the tranny and the brackets.  I can get some cables and a used slave for you, but they will be extra (have to snag them from a junkyard).<P>The Isuzu swap is straight forward......just install it and you're done.  Obviously you should do a clutch job at this time, so factor that in.<P>LMK if you are interested and we'll work things out.<P>  ||||reg||1
Z||000012||ig88vsbobafett||12-29-2001||05:18 PM||||Hey dose the cluch out of a 4 speed work and how much extra is the Cables (And what ever else i would need ??? <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000013||mrfiero||12-29-2001||06:15 PM||||I'm not sure about the clutch......it may work.  If it shows any signs of wear I would replace it.  Since the tranny will be out it is the ideal time to do a clutch job and it will save you the hassle of doing it again in the near future.  I might have a decent used clutch from an Isuzu somewhere, so I can throw that in too, if you want it.<P>I actually have a slave cylinder (used) that I will include in the $50 price.  I can't guarantee that it will work or how long it will last, but at least you will have one (your '84s slave is different).<P>The cables will be whatever I have to pay the junkyard for them, but probably less than $20 for the pair.<P>LMK if you are interested.<P>   <P>||||reg||1
Z||000014||ig88vsbobafett||12-29-2001||06:26 PM||||Did the 84s have a cluch Slave cylinder if not what do i need to do (Do i need to ****  any thing ??||||reg||1
Z||000015||ig88vsbobafett||12-29-2001||06:30 PM||||Yeah one more thing i plan or adding a 3.1 Will it bolt right to that to ??||||reg||1
Z||000016||mrfiero||12-29-2001||07:15 PM||||The slave cylinder on your '84 will not work with the Isuzu (or any other) tranny.  It is an '84 only design.<P>Yes, it will bolt up to a 3.1 (as well as a 2.8, 3.4, etc.).  It has the same bolt pattern as all other Fiero trannies (all Fiero trannies are interchangeable).<P> ||||reg||1
